 <p>The pre-registered expectation was that the state token would carry this row at 0.8 or more; it carried 0.04. A one-forward control settled whether the splice was at fault: zeroing the state token moves the action by 0.10 of the gap, replacing it with the control's by 0.17, swapping the image tokens by 0.91. The checkpoint's training config zeroes the state token on a fifth of samples (<code>state_dropout_prob: 0.2</code>); the head learned not to depend on it. R-042 then split the images: wrist 0.88, agent view 0.17, wrist above agent on 10 of 10.</p>
